<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements of Frost signed with a Developer ID certificate (scripts/release/release.sh, SIGNING_MODE=developer-id).
  Builds signed with the self-signed "Frost Local Signing" identity (every Xcode build and SIGNING_MODE=selfsigned)
  use Frost-SelfSigned.entitlements instead: the same set plus one exception. See docs/releasing.md, "Hardened
  Runtime and entitlements".

  Frost runs with the Hardened Runtime and needs no Hardened Runtime exception and no resource-access entitlement:
  - Synthesized CGEvents (HID tap, session tap, window routing through field 0x33): gated by TCC (Accessibility /
    PostEvent), not by an entitlement.
  - Accessibility (reading and pressing other apps' AXUIElements): TCC Accessibility only.
  - ScreenCaptureKit captures and CGWindowList (window titles of other apps): TCC Screen Recording only.
  - No private CoreGraphics / SkyLight (CGS*) calls, no Apple Events, no JIT, no DYLD_* environment variables (the
    FROST_TEST_* hooks are ordinary environment variables, which the Hardened Runtime leaves alone).
  - Sparkle (non-sandboxed host): its helpers (Autoupdate, Updater.app, Installer.xpc, Downloader.xpc) only link
    system libraries and need nothing from the host app; Downloader.xpc keeps its own (empty) entitlements.
  - Library validation stays on: with Developer ID, the app and Sparkle.framework carry the same Team ID.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Not sandboxed: Frost reads and drives other apps' menu bar items. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<false/>
</dict>
</plist>
